# ── ALL of data/ is runtime state — NEVER track — EXCEPT data/bin/ (the static
# tools the server ships). Belt-and-suspenders over the explicit list below so a
# NEW data file (e.g. data/telemetry/) can never be committed by accident. ──
data/*
!data/bin/
data/bin/code
data/bin/editor/
# generated at startup by createStatusHelper() — never track (dirties the tree, blocks git pull)
data/bin/vibespace-status
# downloaded by installRclone()/boot self-heal — a 60MB arch-specific binary must
# never live in git (2.368.9: it did since the one-click-install commit; every pin
# bump would grow public history by 60MB+, and the boot self-heal writing a tracked
# file is the dirty-tree-blocks-git-pull class). Boot reinstalls it when missing.
data/bin/rclone
data/bin/rclone-dl.zip
# heavy-tier release-gate results (scripts/ci.mjs --heavy): <sha>.{green,red,pid,log}
# — local run records, never history. Already covered by data/* above; spelled
# out because a reader looking for "where does the push-blocking marker live"
# should find it named.
data/ci-heavy/
*.nfs*
.agent-context/
data/.agent-hooks-optout
# ── Sensitive runtime state (NEVER track — key files + their ciphertext = plaintext) ──
data/auth.json
data/accounts.json
data/.accounts-key
data/subs/
data/codex-subs/
data/usage-cache/
data/usage-history/
data/codex-models-seen.json
data/mounts.json
data/.mounts-key
data/mount-tokens.json
data/mount-logs/
data/hosts.json
data/ssh/
data/remote-jsonl/
data/session-status.json
data/user-todos.json
data/task-groups.json
data/tasks.json
data/uploads-sync.json
.claude/worktrees/
data/bin/vibespace-agentd.js
data/bin/vibespace-agentd-attach.js
src/lib/build-version.js
# §8 of scripts/test-new-member-wake.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of
# src/server/usage-pool-engine.js beside the real one (they must be SIBLINGS or
# their relative requires do not resolve). They are unlinked on exit and swept
# at start, but a SIGKILL can strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release
# gate REFUSES on, so they can never be allowed to become tree state.
src/server/vs-wake-mut-*.js
src/server/vs-wake-master-ar-*.js
src/vs-wake-mut-*.js
# §18 of scripts/test-readings-attribution.mjs writes a PATCHED COPY of
# src/server/usage-pool-engine.js beside the real one (same reason: relative
# requires). Unlinked on exit, swept by PID at start; a SIGKILL must never be
# able to dirty the tree and block the release gate.
src/server/vs-readattr-mut-*.js
# scripts/test-quota-model.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of the modules under test
# BESIDE the real ones (they must be siblings, or their relative requires do not
# resolve): §⑯ `vs-qmr3-`, §⑰ `vs-qmr4-`, §⑱ `vs-qmr6-` in src/, src/harnesses/
# and src/adapters/. Unlinked on exit, swept by PID at start; a SIGKILL must
# never be able to dirty the tree and block the gate — and §⑰'s prefix was
# missing here for a whole release, so the pattern is now the FAMILY (no slash ⇒
# any directory) rather than one line per section, and §⑱0 asks git itself
# whether every path this suite can write is ignored.
vs-qm*-mut-*.js
# scripts/test-auto-resume.mjs §12a writes PATCHED COPIES of
# src/server/auto-resume.js beside the real one (they must be SIBLINGS or their
# relative requires do not resolve). Unlinked on exit and swept at start, but a
# SIGKILL can strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on.
src/server/vs-aredge-mut-*.js
# §8 of scripts/test-desktop-app-keeper.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of
# src/server/desktop-app-keeper.js beside the real one (they must be SIBLINGS
# or their relative requires do not resolve) as the negative controls for the
# r2 findings. Unlinked on exit and swept by PID at start, but a SIGKILL can
# strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on.
src/server/vs-dak-mut-*.js
# §5 (f) of scripts/test-desktop-display.mjs: a patched copy of src/desktop-display.js
# (the pre-fix xpra argv/env) as the lifecycle legs' negative control — same rules.
src/vs-dd-mut-*.js

# §5c of scripts/test-spend-paths.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of
# src/server/conversation-deliver.js beside the real one (SIBLINGS, or their
# relative requires do not resolve). Unlinked on exit and swept by PID at
# start, but a SIGKILL can strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release
# gate REFUSES on.
src/server/vs-spend-mut-*.js
# throwaway patched copies of src/server/session-stdout.js written BESIDE the
# real module by scripts/test-restore-liveness.mjs (they must be SIBLINGS or
# their relative requires do not resolve). Unlinked on exit, but a SIGKILL can
# strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on.
src/server/session-stdout.__*_control.js
# scripts/test-browser-resources.mjs (§ⓔ) and scripts/test-browser-profiles.mjs
# (§⑬) write PATCHED COPIES of src/server/browser-env.js beside the real one as
# their PRE-FIX controls (SIBLINGS, or their relative requires do not resolve).
# Unlinked on exit and swept by PID at start, but a SIGKILL can strand one —
# and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on.
src/server/vs-browser-mut-*.js
# scripts/test-queue-steer.mjs (⑬d and the r3 negative controls) writes PATCHED COPIES of src/lib/chat-view.js — `.chat-view.prefix-<pid>.js` AND `.chat-view.stale-prefix-<pid>-*.js` (2.369.83: the merge verifier found the first name uncovered)
# beside the real one (they must be SIBLINGS or their relative imports do not
# resolve). They are unlinked on exit and swept at start, but a SIGKILL can
# strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on, so they can
# never be allowed to become tree state.
src/lib/.chat-view.*prefix-*.js

# scripts/test-discovery-spawn.mjs writes a PRE-FIX COPY of src/session-store.js
# (`git show master:…`) beside the real one as its NEGATIVE CONTROL — they must
# be SIBLINGS or that module's relative requires do not resolve. It is unlinked
# on exit and swept by PID LIVENESS at start (a concurrent run of the same
# suite in this worktree must keep its own copy), but a SIGKILL can strand one
# — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on, so it can never be
# allowed to become tree state.
src/.session-store.spawnfix-*.js

# scripts/test-fable-cap-pool-storm.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of
# src/account-pool-auto.js and src/server/usage-pool-engine.js BESIDE the real
# ones (they must be SIBLINGS or their relative requires do not resolve).
# Unlinked on exit and swept by PID at start, but a SIGKILL can strand one —
# and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on, so they can never be
# allowed to become tree state. The pattern is the FAMILY (no slash ⇒ any
# directory) because the copies land in two of them.
vs-fable-mut-*.js

# scripts/test-channel-store.mjs writes a PRE-FIX COPY of src/channel-store.js
# (`.channel-store.prefix-<pid>.js`) BESIDE the real one as its NEGATIVE
# CONTROL — it must be a SIBLING or that module's relative requires do not
# resolve. It is unlinked on exit and swept by PID LIVENESS at start (a
# concurrent run of the same suite in this worktree must keep its own copy),
# but a SIGKILL can strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate
# REFUSES on, so it can never be allowed to become tree state.
src/.channel-store.prefix-*.js
# and scripts/test-channels-engine.mjs writes PATCHED COPIES of BOTH
# src/channel-store.js and src/server/channels-engine.js beside the real ones,
# for the same reason and with the same hazard. Each control gets its OWN name
# (node caches modules by resolved path, so two controls sharing a filename
# silently drive the first patch twice).
src/server/.channels-engine.prefix-*.js
# …and (channels r3) patched copies of the adapter REGISTRY and the FAKE
# adapter beside them, because the pre-fix scan-lane control needs all three
# pieces of the r2 shape wired to each other.
src/channels/.index.prefix-*.js
src/channels/.fake.prefix-*.js
# scripts/test-secret-box.mjs writes a PATCHED COPY of the PRE-FIX mounts
# `_key()`/`_enc()`/`_dec()` beside the real module (`src/.mounts-legacy-enc.prefix-<pid>.js`)
# as its parity + bare-catch negative control, and scripts/test-integration-registry.mjs
# writes PRE-FIX copies of the store (`src/server/.integration-store.prefix-<pid>-*.js`)
# for its controls. Unlinked on exit and swept at start by PID liveness, but a
# SIGKILL can strand one — and a dirty tree is what the release gate REFUSES on.
src/.mounts-legacy-enc.prefix-*.js
src/server/.integration-store.prefix-*.js
